+## Sales and variance
+
+`POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+`ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant with a time zone,
+`qty` a whole number above zero). Each dish sold uses one portion of its
+recipe per `qty`, consumed at `soldAt` with the ledger `ref` `sale:<ticket>`.
+Tickets imported before are skipped. The answer is
+`{ "tickets": <new tickets>, "dishes": <dishes sold on them, summed qty> }`.
+If any row is invalid (`bad_request`) or an item runs out
+(`import_out_of_stock`, 409), nothing is imported and the message names the
+row (`row 2` is the first data row).
+
+`GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists per item
+`{ itemId, name, unit, theoretical, actual, difference }`: theoretical use
+from sales sold in those days (inclusive), actual use from every `consume`
+movement in those days, and `difference = actual - theoretical`. Items where
+both are zero are left out.
